@style(../styles/IDocDemo.style)
@title(Octo 7: 3-D plots and animation)

Every 3-D figure can be turned with the mouse. A loop that redraws with `drawnow` or `pause` becomes an animation the reader can play.

@section(Grids and surfaces)

`meshgrid` turns two vectors into coordinate grids; `surf` and `mesh` draw a height over them.

@octo
[X, Y] = meshgrid(-2:0.2:2);
Z = X .* exp(-X.^2 - Y.^2);
surf(X, Y, Z); title("surf"); xlabel("x"); ylabel("y"); zlabel("z"); colorbar;
figure; mesh(X, Y, Z); title("mesh");
figure; contour(X, Y, Z, 12); title("contour");
figure; contourf(X, Y, Z); title("contourf");
figure; imagesc(Z); colormap(jet); title("imagesc");
@end

@section(Curves, points and vector fields)

`plot3` and `scatter3` work in three coordinates; `quiver` draws arrows; `lighting`, `material` and `camlight` light a surface.

@octo
t = linspace(0, 6*pi, 300);
plot3(cos(t), sin(t), t / 6); title("helix"); view(45, 30);
figure; scatter3(randn(1, 60), randn(1, 60), randn(1, 60)); title("scatter3");
figure; [x, y] = meshgrid(-1:0.25:1); quiver(x, y, -y, x); title("rotation field");
figure; [x, y, z] = sphere(20); surf(x, y, z); axis equal; shading interp; title("sphere");
figure; [X, Y] = meshgrid(-2:0.4:2); Z = X .* exp(-X.^2 - Y.^2);
meshc(X, Y, Z); title("meshc: mesh with contours");
figure; surfc(X, Y, Z); title("surfc");
figure; waterfall(X, Y, Z); title("waterfall");
figure; surface(X, Y, Z); title("surface");
figure; surf(X, Y, Z); shading interp; lighting gouraud; material shiny; camlight; title("lit surface");
@end

@section(Animation)

Clear and redraw inside a loop; `pause(s)` holds each frame for s seconds, `drawnow` takes a frame at once.

@octo
x = linspace(0, 2*pi, 80);
for k = 1:24
  clf;
  plot(x, sin(x - k * pi / 12), "LineWidth", 2);
  axis([0 2*pi -1 1]);
  title(sprintf("travelling wave, frame %d", k));
  pause(0.05);
end
@end

@octo
[X, Y] = meshgrid(-3:0.25:3);
for k = 1:12
  clf;
  surf(X, Y, sin(sqrt(X.^2 + Y.^2) - k / 2));
  zlim([-1 1]); title("ripple");
  drawnow;
end
@end
